  "answer_text": "The URL **`www.home.fedex.com/express`** (or simply `home.fedex.com`) is the **internal intranet homepage** for FedEx Express employees. \n\n### Key Points to Know:\n* **Access Restricted:** Because this is an internal portal, it is secured behind the FedEx corporate firewall. **You cannot access this website from a personal device or a standard home internet connection.**\n* **How to Open It:** To load this page, you must be connected to the internal FedEx network. This means you must be on-site using a company-authorized work computer or logged in via an approved corporate VPN.\n* **What It's Used For:** On-site employees use this homepage to search \"Keywords\" to access tools like *Dimensions* (to view/edit timecards), internal job postings, corporate policies, and benefit programs.\n\n### How to Access Employee Info from Home:\nIf you are at home and trying to check your work schedule, view your pay stubs, or manage HR information, you cannot use the `home.fedex.com` link. Instead, you should use FedEx's public-facing external employee tools:\n\n1. **FedEx Workday / PurpleID:** You can log into your Workday account or Okta portal on a personal computer or mobile device to view your personal profile and hours.\n2. **ADP (or Regional Payroll Portal):** For pay stubs and tax documents, log in directly via the ADP website or the respective payroll portal recommended by your station.\n3. **Contact Your Manager:** If you do not have the direct, external login links for your specific division (Express, Ground, etc.), ask your manager or HR representative for the off-site login instructions.",
